1:1 COMMENT "# list_slice.z -- `slice from: to:` is the list twin of `substring`: a"
1:71 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# half-open [from, to) window over the SAME storage, built as a length and a"
2:77 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# pointer advance. It allocates nothing and copies nothing."
3:60 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "#"
4:2 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# Slicing an owner pins it SHARED, so several slices of one list coexist and"
5:77 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# the list stays readable; a writer is excluded, because `append` may realloc."
6:79 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# Slicing a slice pins nothing further -- a view is value-passed and carries"
7:77 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# nothing that can dangle."
8:27 EOL "\n"
9:1 EOL "\n"
